R40	Cueing Arg1:T29 Arg2:T27	
R41	Addressee Arg1:T30 Arg2:T27	
T31	Quotation 3220 3438	"It was from the reigning family of Holland, though the matter in which I served them was of such delicacy that I cannot confide it even to you, who have been good enough to chronicle one or two of my little problems."
R42	Speaker Arg1:T30 Arg2:T31	
R43	Addressee Arg1:T28 Arg2:T31	
T32	Quotation 3439 3475	"And have you any on hand just now?"
T33	Entity 3476 3477	I
T34	Cue 3478 3483	asked
R44	Speaker Arg1:T33 Arg2:T32	
R45	Cueing Arg1:T34 Arg2:T32	
R46	Addressee Arg1:T30 Arg2:T32	
T35	Quotation 3499 4246	"Some ten or twelve, but none which present any feature of interest. They are important, you understand, without being interesting. Indeed, I have found that it is usually in unimportant matters that there is a field for the observation, and for the quick analysis of cause and effect which gives the charm to an investigation. The larger crimes are apt to be the simpler, for the bigger the crime the more obvious, as a rule, is the motive. In these cases, save for one rather intricate matter which has been referred to me from Marseilles, there is nothing which presents any features of interest. It is possible, however, that I may have something better before very many minutes are over, for this is one of my clients, or I am much mistaken."
T36	Entity 4247 4249	He
R47	Speaker Arg1:T36 Arg2:T35	
R48	Addressee Arg1:T33 Arg2:T35	
T37	Quotation 4957 4993	"I have seen those symptoms before,"
T38	Cue 4994 4998	said
T39	Entity 4999 5005	Holmes
R49	Cueing Arg1:T38 Arg2:T37	
R50	Speaker Arg1:T39 Arg2:T37	
R51	Addressee Arg1:T33 Arg2:T37	
T40	Quotation 5045 5531	"Oscillation upon the pavement always means an affaire de coeur. She would like advice, but is not sure that the matter is not too delicate for communication. And yet even here we may discriminate. When a woman has been seriously wronged by a man she no longer oscillates, and the usual symptom is a broken bell wire. Here we may take it that there is a love matter, but that the maiden is not so much angry as perplexed, or grieved. But here she comes in person to resolve our doubts."
