R136	Addressee Arg1:T90 Arg2:T98	
T99	Quotation 11162 11435	"Yes, sir. I met him that night, and he called next day to ask if we had got home all safe, and after that we met him-- that is to say, Mr. Holmes, I met him twice for walks, but after that father came back again, and Mr. Hosmer Angel could not come to the house any more."
R137	Addressee Arg1:T95 Arg2:T99	
R138	Speaker Arg1:T90 Arg2:T99	
T100	Quotation 11436 11441	"No?"
R139	Speaker Arg1:T95 Arg2:T100	
R140	Addressee Arg1:T90 Arg2:T100	
T101	Quotation 11442 11734	"Well, you know father didn't like anything of the sort. He wouldn't have any visitors if he could help it, and he used to say that a woman should be happy in her own family circle. But then, as I used to say to mother, a woman wants her own circle to begin with, and I had not got mine yet."
R141	Addressee Arg1:T95 Arg2:T101	
R142	Speaker Arg1:T90 Arg2:T101	
