R289	Cueing Arg1:T198 Arg2:T196	
R290	Addressee Arg1:T193 Arg2:T196	
T199	Quotation 23835 24123	"Not only that, but the signature is typewritten. Look at the neat little 'Hosmer Angel' at the bottom. There is a date, you see, but no superscription except Leadenhall Street, which is rather vague. The point about the signature is very suggestive --in fact, we may call it conclusive."
R291	Addressee Arg1:T197 Arg2:T199	
R292	Speaker Arg1:T193 Arg2:T199	
T200	Quotation 24124 24134	"Of what?"
R293	Speaker Arg1:T197 Arg2:T200	
R294	Addressee Arg1:T193 Arg2:T200	
T201	Quotation 24135 24219	"My dear fellow, is it possible you do not see how strongly it bears upon the case?"
R295	Addressee Arg1:T197 Arg2:T201	
R296	Speaker Arg1:T193 Arg2:T201	
T202	Quotation 24220 24359	"I cannot say that I do unless it were that he wished to be able to deny his signature if an action for breach of promise were instituted."
R297	Speaker Arg1:T197 Arg2:T202	
R298	Addressee Arg1:T193 Arg2:T202	
T203	Quotation 24360 24833	"No, that was not the point. However, I shall write two letters, which should settle the matter. One is to a firm in the City, the other is to the young lady's stepfather, Mr. Windibank, asking him whether he could meet us here at six o'clock tomorrow evening. It is just as well that we should do business with the male relatives. And now, Doctor, we can do nothing until the answers to those letters come, so we may put our little problem upon the shelf for the interim."
R299	Addressee Arg1:T197 Arg2:T203	
R300	Speaker Arg1:T193 Arg2:T203	
T204	Quotation 26366 26393	"Well, have you solved it?"
T205	Entity 26394 26395	I
T206	Entity 26298 26300	he
T207	Cue 26396 26401	asked
R301	Speaker Arg1:T205 Arg2:T204	
R302	Cueing Arg1:T207 Arg2:T204	
R303	Addressee Arg1:T206 Arg2:T204	
T208	Quotation 26416 26455	"Yes. It was the bisulphate of baryta."
R304	Addressee Arg1:T205 Arg2:T208	
R305	Speaker Arg1:T206 Arg2:T208	
T209	Quotation 26456 26478	"No, no, the mystery!"
T210	Entity 26479 26480	I
T211	Cue 26481 26486	cried
