R315	Cueing Arg1:T215 Arg2:T217	
R316	Speaker Arg1:T216 Arg2:T217	
R317	Addressee Arg1:T210 Arg2:T217	
T218	Quotation 27467 27503	"Good-evening, Mr. James Windibank,"
T219	Cue 27504 27508	said
T220	Entity 27509 27515	Holmes
R318	Cueing Arg1:T219 Arg2:T218	
R319	Speaker Arg1:T220 Arg2:T218	
T221	Quotation 27517 27626	"I think that this typewritten letter is from you, in which you made an appointment with me for six o'clock?"
T222	Entity 27320 27322	He
R320	Cueing Arg1:T219 Arg2:T221	
R321	Speaker Arg1:T220 Arg2:T221	
R322	Addressee Arg1:T222 Arg2:T218	
R323	Addressee Arg1:T222 Arg2:T221	
T223	Quotation 27627 28306	"Yes, sir. I am afraid that I am a little late, but I am not quite my own master, you know. I am sorry that Miss Sutherland has troubled you about this little matter, for I think it is far better not to wash linen of the sort in public. It was quite against my wishes that she came, but she is a very excitable, impulsive girl, as you may have noticed, and she is not easily controlled when she has made up her mind on a point. Of course, I did not mind you so much, as you are not connected with the official police, but it is not pleasant to have a family misfortune like this noised abroad. Besides, it is a useless expense, for how could you possibly find this Hosmer Angel?"
R324	Addressee Arg1:T220 Arg2:T223	
R325	Speaker Arg1:T222 Arg2:T223	
T224	Quotation 28307 28325	"On the contrary,"
T225	Cue 28326 28330	said
T226	Entity 28331 28337	Holmes
T227	Quotation 28347 28432	"I have every reason to believe that I will succeed in discovering Mr. Hosmer Angel."
R326	Speaker Arg1:T226 Arg2:T227	
