R330	Addressee Arg1:T228 Arg2:T224	
R331	Addressee Arg1:T228 Arg2:T227	
T229	Quotation 28492 28520	"I am delighted to hear it,"
T230	Entity 28521 28523	he
T231	Cue 28524 28528	said
R332	Speaker Arg1:T230 Arg2:T229	
R333	Cueing Arg1:T231 Arg2:T229	
R334	Addressee Arg1:T226 Arg2:T229	
T232	Quotation 28530 28554	"It is a curious thing,"
T233	Cue 28555 28563	remarked
T234	Entity 28564 28570	Holmes
T235	Quotation 28572 29027	"that a typewriter has really quite as much individuality as a man's handwriting. Unless they are quite new, no two of them write exactly alike. Some letters get more worn than others, and some wear only on one side. Now, you remark in this note of yours, Mr. Windibank, that in every case there is some little slurring over of the 'e,' and a slight defect in the tail of the 'r.' There are fourteen other characteristics, but those are the more obvious."
R335	Cueing Arg1:T233 Arg2:T232	
R336	Speaker Arg1:T234 Arg2:T232	
